{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And Moses said, six hundred.</b> And people raise the difficulty: how could it enter Moses' mind to say this thing? Did he not know that it was in the power of the Holy One, blessed be He, to supply their request? And the Gaon our Rabbi Nissim explained: this is what it says: ״ויאמר משה שש מאות אלף רגלי העם אשר אנכי בקרבו״ — meaning, they are a great people, ״ואתה אמרת בשר אתן להם ואכלו חדש ימים״ — meaning, You said it in anger and in wrath, as it is written ״עד אשר יצא מאפכם״ — ״בשר אתן להם ביום אחד כדי לאכול חדש ימים״. ״הצאן ובקר ישחט להם״ — meaning, regarding what You said to supply, I know that ״כל תוכל״ — but what is upon man to do, what will it be? Can human beings gather in a single day enough for six hundred thousand footmen for a month? ״ואם כל דגי הים יאסף״ — meaning, if all the fish of the sea were caught in a net and they needed only to gather them — could they gather them in a single day for the need of a month?"], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:14.489840767Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}